  "id": "non-rem-sleep",
  "term": "non-REM sleep",
  "definition": "Non-REM sleep is a sleep state contrasted with REM sleep in which mental activity is described as showing more secondary-process features. In this source, awakenings from non-REM sleep were linked with more conceptual associations and less primary-process-style rebus thinking than REM sleep.",
